Make a new file and insert this code:

#!/bin/bash
echo "--File Reader--"
read_file="file.txt"
if [ -f "$read_file" ]; then
    echo "File exists: $read_file"
    cat "$read_file"
else
    echo "Error: File not found!"
fi

Save this as anything you want but it has to be a file with the '.sh' extension.
Make a file named 'file.txt', for example.
In the shell command prompt, run these commands:

chmod +x [yourfilename].sh
./[yourfilename].sh

Check if it prints the content of the 'file.txt' file.
